# "run loop" = the site queue

When Matt says **run loop**, **run the loop**, **go**, or **keep going until the site is
done**, he means the site queue. Not the growth loop, not an audit, not a plan
(Matt 2026-09-09: "run loop" never flips to another skill).

**Read first:** `.cursor/skills/site-queue/SKILL.md` — the pointer skill for a non-Claude
builder, which names the canonical protocol (`.claude/skills/site-queue/SKILL.md`) and the
four mission documents. Then work. Do not re-audit the site; the backlog already exists.

## The three commands

```bash
npx tsx scripts/site-queue-status.ts --json                                    # what to take, in serve order
npx tsx scripts/site-queue-status.ts --claim SITE-XX,SITE-YY --owner <owner>   # the ONLY claim path
npx tsx scripts/site-queue-status.ts --touch SITE-XX,SITE-YY --owner <owner>   # hourly, while you hold
```

`--json` carries `liveWorkers`, `maxWorkers` and `staleClaims`. **If `liveWorkers` is at or
above `maxWorkers` (3), stop and say so** — every worker spends one shared account
allowance, and four at once exhausted it and killed all of them on 2026-09-08. Otherwise
claim the first two eligible items in the JSON's order on disjoint file sets. A non-zero
exit means you got nothing: read the message, do not hand-write a claim. Claude sessions
and Grok sessions coexist by this tool alone; never coordinate by hand.

Owner name: `grok-<model>-<YYYY-MM-DD>`, or `cursor-<model>-<date>`. A claim whose
heartbeat is older than three hours is released to the next worker, so heartbeat hourly or
lose the node.

## The bar

Every SITE node's accept test ends the same way: a **separate evaluator** — a different
model from the builder — scores the page class from shots at 1440 and 375
(`scripts/take-route-shots.mjs`), three scorings in one call, median, and the score must
rise. Receipt in the route's `parity.json` per `design_system/public/TASTE.md`, shape
checked by `scripts/lib/taste-receipt.mjs`. The instrument is **grok-4.6** through the `grok`
CLI (Matt's Grok subscription, not API credit) — the same judge for every builder, so marks
stay comparable. Run it with `npx tsx scripts/taste-evaluate.ts <route-key>`. A Grok lane
builds with **grok-4.5**, because the gate refuses a model grading its own page. **Finish line: every public
page class at 70 or above on that table** (Matt 2026-09-09).

Then the gates (`npm run ci:gates`), the `Node: <id>` trailer on every commit touching
`app/**` or `components/site/**` (G72), ONE `npm run push` per round from the main
checkout, `deploy:verify`, a live check on ryan-realty.com, and the evidence written on
the node — done, or blocked with `blocked_until` so it reopens itself, or blocked on Matt
with the question in ONE line in `blocked_reason`.

## Never

- Never wait on Matt mid-round: take the safe path the skill allows, write what you chose
  on the node, keep going.
- Never mark a node done from a self-report; evidence is what the environment showed.
- Never leave finished work on a branch — merge and push, or write it into
  `docs/plans/CROSS_AGENT_HANDOFF.md` before you stop.
